1
00:00:01,611 --> 00:00:06,572
Meta, the parent company of Facebook, is
reportedly planning to build a $10 billion

2
00:00:06,773 --> 00:00:10,433
underwater fiber optic cable that will go
around the world.

3
00:00:10,913 --> 00:00:14,054
The cable would help the company handle
high user traffic

4
00:00:14,434 --> 00:00:17,035
and keep a high quality of service
internationally.

5
00:00:17,475 --> 00:00:21,156
It also brings Meta in line with Alphabet,
the parent company of Google.

6
00:00:21,596 --> 00:00:26,317
Alphabet and Google have a network of
cables, some of which they own fully.

7
00:00:26,657 --> 00:00:29,398
The technology news site TechCrunch
reported

8
00:00:29,718 --> 00:00:32,819
that it would be a cable exclusively for
the company's use

9
00:00:33,179 --> 00:00:37,081
and would avoid areas they think face
political and military tensions.

10
00:00:37,661 --> 00:00:41,762
The reported route for the cable will take
it from the east coast of the U.S.,

11
00:00:42,162 --> 00:00:45,703
across the Atlantic around South Africa,
up to India,

12
00:00:45,863 --> 00:00:50,105
above the northern part of Australia, and
across the Pacific to the west coast.

13
00:00:50,725 --> 00:00:54,887
Undersea cables play a key role in global
fiber optic internet,

14
00:00:55,228 --> 00:00:58,689
but their locations can put them at risk.
Cables in the Red

15
00:00:58,789 --> 00:01:01,931
Sea suffered damage from strikes by
Yemen's Houthi rebels.

16
00:01:02,512 --> 00:01:03,812
And authorities in Denmark

17
00:01:03,992 --> 00:01:09,255
have been looking into cable damage caused
in the Baltic Sea by a Chinese ship.

18
00:01:09,715 --> 00:01:13,057
They accused the crew of the ship, which
left from a Russian port,

19
00:01:13,237 --> 00:01:17,380
of intentionally dragging its anchor to
cut underwater cables.

20
00:01:18,120 --> 00:01:20,881
The TechCrunch report says Meta will
likely share more

21
00:01:21,001 --> 00:01:25,122
details about its global project sometime
in 2025

22
00:01:25,542 --> 00:01:30,003
and that the project could take years to
complete. For Straight Arrow News,

23
